Usability Specifications 

1.Stress-Reducing Palette(Passive):  Site-wide layout. Cool blue/slate (#2C3E50), high contrast (7:1 ratio). This is for those with Visual Impairments / Cognitive Anxiety. Prevents visual fatigue and maintains a calm aesthetic during timed pressure. 
2.Constructive Feedback Cards(Active): Results Dashboard. Centralized container, green/amber indicators. For those who require Cognitive Support / Neurodivergent Users. Frames performance constructively around specs to build confidence. 
3.Minimalist Exam Workspace(Passive): Past Paper Interface. High padding, zero side banners/popups. For those who require support with Focus / ADHD.  Eliminates visual clutter so students focus purely on exam questions. 
4.Subtle Progress Bar(Active): Header Bar. Horizontal 4px bar, smooth transition. To ensure students go through minimum Stress Time Monitoring.  Replaces flashing timers with non-intrusive visual progress cues. 
5.Keyboard-First Navigation(Active): Exam Screen. Shortcuts (`Alt+N` Next, `Alt+P` Previous). For those with Motor Impairments / Power Users. Allows for seamless navigation without forcing trackpad reliance. |
6.Scalable Text Control( Active):Main Control Bar. Adjustable font scaling (14px–24px). For those with Visual Impairments / Low Vision. Ensures text readability across varying screen resolutions. |
7.Auto-Save Draft Engine(Active): Input Fields. Triggers every 5 seconds locally.to ensure  Error Prevention / Data Loss. This feature Protects student work against accidental browser refreshes or disconnects. 
8.High-Contrast Mark Badges(Passive): Next to question text. Rounded pill boxes, bold typography. Clear Information Hierarchy. Instantly displays mark allocation so students budget time effectively. 
9.Screen-Reader Labels(Passive): All interactive DOM nodes. Full `aria-label` tags. For those with  Visual Impairments / Screen Readers. This Ensures that accessibility tools parse input boxes and timer alerts cleanly. 
10.Explicit Confirmation Modals(Active): Paper Submission. Dual-action popup ("Confirm Finish"). This Prevents accidental paper submissions before all questions are complete. 

